# Golden trace: Linux btusb (kernel 7.3.1-1-cachyos) setting up the Helios 300
# BT chip 04ca:3016 after its USB port was power-cycled (usb1-port7/disable
# 1 -> 0) on 2026-11-08. The chip kept its rampatch (status 0xe0), so Linux
# sends GET_TARGET_VERSION, CHECK_STATUS, GET_TARGET_VERSION and no download.
# Captured with tools/linux/usbmon_pcap.c, reduced with tools/usbmon_reduce.py
# (device 4 on bus 1). HCI events/ACL data are not included.
# replay: allow-extra-final-status
#   (our core adds one read-only CHECK_STATUS after Linux's sequence)
